    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.completion\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! I had one more doubt. Is it possible to disable buffer word completion for files larger than lets say 1MB. Is there any functionality like this or are there any hacky ways to implement this. The issue is that for a fairly large file, I am testing this with sqlite.c(8.7MB C code) amalgamation file btw, the editor hangs a lot because mini.completion has to process buffer words and show it in completion-menu afaik and see. Is something of this sort really possible with mini.completion.",
    "closed_at": "2024-08-22T18:07:50Z",
    "closed_by": {
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?v=4",
