    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The \"buffer word\" completion is a result of applying [fallback action](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a8185957febe7dae31556dbd7326cfa597b812f1/doc/mini-completion.txt#L213), which indeed is synchronous and can result into lag.\r\n\r\nWhat can probably be done here is to set [buffer-local config](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a8185957febe7dae31556dbd7326cfa597b812f1/doc/mini-completion.txt#L63-L65) to disable fallback action in particular buffer. Like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.b.minicompletion_config = { fallback_action = function() end }\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen and how this is set is left for user to decide. For example, you can set this in autocommand for `BufAdd` event after checking that file size (or line number) is too big.\r\n\r\nOne thing to know, though, is that this fallback action (similarly to built-in `<C-n>`) checks **all** opened buffers. So disabling it in only big one might not be enough, because as long as there is a big buffer open, it will be scanned in other buffers.",
