        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> One thing to know, though, is that this fallback action (similarly to built-in `<C-n>`) checks **all** opened buffers. So disabling it in only big one might not be enough, because as long as there is a big buffer open, it will be scanned in other buffers.\r\n\r\n@echasnovski, can we use `complete` to do something like ``set complete=.`` so that the it only uses current buffer for completion. Is that possible? Does this effect how mini.completion fallback mechanism works.",
